From 00acf91e74f48767a86ecb6678b594dd94acd868 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toemmsen96 <147745097+Toemmsen96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:45:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: C-PHY on SM8450

Add the C-PHY lane sequence of the SM8450 CSIPHY (v2.1.0) and select the
PHY type in CSID 680, on top of the C-PHY series.

The sequence is the downstream camera-kernel's csiphy_3ph_v2_1_0_reg for
the three trios followed by its data rate entries for up to 2.1 Gsps
(downstream picks the first bucket whose bandwidth covers the rate), with
the common control writes it does in reset exit and common config: CTRL0
0x0e and CTRL7 0x7a. CSID 680 has the PHY type select at bit 24 of
CSI2_RX_CFG0 like gen2.

Tested on the Xiaomi 12 main camera (Sony IMX766, three trios at 1713.6
Msps into CSIPHY2): colour bars and real frames at 4096x3072.

Signed-off-by: Toemmsen96 <147745097+Toemmsen96@users.noreply.github.com>
---
